$ hql help round
fn round(self: Float) : Float    // std/math

    The whole number nearest `self`, as a `Float`; a value halfway between
    two rounds away from zero: `2.5f | round` is `3.0`.

fn round(self: Decimal) : Decimal    // std/math
fn round(self: Decimal, places: Int) : Decimal    // std/math

    `self` rounded half to even to `places` digits after the point, and
    kept at that scale: `round(2.345, 2)` is `2.34`, and `round(x)` is
    `round(x, 0)`. See Division and rounding <https://hql.hypermarkdown.org/v{version}/learn/02-data-types/decimal/#division-and-rounding>.
